Common Kubernetes Upgrade Mistakes (Avoid These!) 🚨

Many cluster failures happen not because of upgrade, but because of these mistakes 👇

1. Skipping Minor Versions

Example: 1.26 → 1.29 

Always upgrade one minor version at a time 

 2. No Backup Before Upgrade

No etcd backup = high risk

Always take backup before touching production

 3. Upgrading Worker Nodes First

Control Plane must always be upgraded first

Workers depend on Control Plane APIs

 4. Not Draining Nodes

Pods may crash or face downtime

Always drain nodes safely

 5. Ignoring Deprecated APIs

Old APIs may stop working

Check kubectl api-resources & release notes

6. No Monitoring After Upgrade

Issues may appear after some time

Always check logs, metrics & alerts

 7. Direct Production Upgrade

Never upgrade prod without testing

Always test in dev/stage first

 Golden Upgrade Checklist

 Backup done
 Release notes checked
 Control plane upgraded
 Nodes upgraded one by one
 Monitoring enabled

A safe Kubernetes upgrade is all about planning, patience, and practice.
